  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, and the new tests pass along with the rest of `tests/test_types.py` (47 passed, 2 skipped). I did not run the full suite.\n\n- **Parsing:** `key=value` becomes `(key, value)`, split on the first `=`. So `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- **Failures:** input without `=` or with an empty key fails with `'<value>' is not a valid key=value pair.`.\n- **Code:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` and exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Tests:** two new tests in `tests/test_types.py` cover valid pairs and the failure cases.\n\nI did not update `CHANGES.md` or `docs/`, which `CLAUDE.md` asks for on user-visible changes. The only version section in `CHANGES.md` is the already-released 8.5.0, and I didn't want to guess where an unreleased entry belongs. Tell me the section to use and I'll add the entry and a docs note.",
